essment': {'usage_kind': 'protocol', 'evidence': ['setupSsl builds an SSLContext via SSLContext.getInstance("TLS") and calls init(arrayOf(clientKeyManager), arrayOf(trustManager), null); the TrustManager comes from a branch on trustAllCerts.', 'When trustAllCerts is true, trustManager is an anonymous application-defined X509TrustManager whose checkClientTrusted and checkServerTrusted do nothing (accept every chain) and getAcceptedIssuers returns an empty array.', 'When trustAllCerts is false, trustManager is Platform.get().platformTrustManager() (a validating platform manager, not an application-defined class).', 'cachingHttpClient declares trustAllCerts: Boolean = true as its default, and calls setupSsl when a client certificate alias is non-blank or trustAllCerts is true; ProviderAPI calls cachingHttpClient without passing trustAllCerts, so it gets the accept-all default.', 'provideOkHttpClient also calls cachingHttpClient without trustAllCerts, so the singleton OkHttpClient also defaults to the accept-all manager.', 'At runtime in 2 runs, the TrustManager[] given to init contained the application class OkHttpClientModuleKt$setupSsl$trustManager$2 and no TrustManagerFactory origin was observed.', 'The statement hostnameVerifier { _, _ -> true } inside the trustAllCerts branch is evaluated as a Kotlin expression statement on the builder, which installs an accept-all hostname verifier on the OkHttpClient.Builder receiver in that branch.', 'Hosts are user-configured (server URL entered in account dialogs), so no root for them can be bundled.'], 'legacy_compatibility_required': True, 'safe_strategy': 'Keep SSLContext.getInstance("TLS") negotiation and pin no protocol version. OkHttp\'s default MODERN_TLS spec already excludes deprecated protocols. The platform TrustManager and default hostname verification apply by default. The network security config provided by the pipeline allows user-installed CAs.', 'policy_authorized': True}, 'publication_considerations': [{'category': 'maintainer_decision', 'description': 'Making validation the default rejects self-signed or private-CA servers that were silently accepted before. The reviewer must confirm this is acceptable for self-hosted users. The added network security config lets them install their CA on the device.', 'kind': 'user_configured_server_trust', 'supporting_claim_ids': ['C4', 'C5', 'C9']}, {'category': 'runtime_behavior', 'description': 'Behaviour against real user-configured servers (self-signed, private CA, user-installed CA via the network security config) shows only on a device. The patch must keep client-certificate support and the explicit accept-all branch working.', 'kind': 'device_tls_behavior', 'supporting_claim_ids': ['C4', 'C6']}, {'category': 'analyzer_reconfirmation', 'description': 'The detector may still flag the platformTrustManager() result as not coming from a TrustManagerFactory. This is a note for the reviewer, not something this validation can show.', 'kind': 'analyzer_reconfirmation', 'supporting_claim_ids': ['C3', 'C6']}], 'publication_blocker_record': {'decision': 'MULTI_FILE_FIX_PROPOSED_FOR_REVIEW', 'blockers': [{'category': 'maintainer_decision', 'kind': 'user_configured_server_trust', 'description': 'Making validation the default rejects self-signed or private-CA servers that were silently accepted before. The reviewer must confirm this is acceptable for self-hosted users. The added network security config lets them install their CA on the device.', 'discharged_by_pipeline_validation': False}, {'category': 'runtime_behavior', 'kind': 'device_tls_behavior', 'description': 'Behaviour against real user-configured servers (self-signed, private CA, user-installed CA via the network security config) shows only on a device. The patch must keep client-certificate support and the explicit accept-all branch working.', 'discharged_by_pipeline_validation': False}, {'category': 'analyzer_reconfirmation', 'kind': 'analyzer_reconfirmation', 'description': 'The detector may still flag the platformTrustManager() result as not coming from a TrustManagerFactory. This is a note for the reviewer, not something this validation can show.', 'discharged_by_pipeline_validation': False}], 'discharged_blockers': [], 'evidence_gap_promoted': [], 'plan_publication_blockers': ["Maintainer decision: validation by default rejects self-signed or private-CA servers that were accepted silently before; self-hosted users must install their CA on the device (the pipeline's network security config allows user-installed CAs). The reviewer must confirm this is acceptable.", 'Runtime behaviour against real user-configured servers (self-signed, private CA, client certificate) can only be checked on a device.', 'Reviewer note: the detector may still flag the platformTrustManager() result as not coming from a TrustManagerFactory.', 'Reviewer note: no caller was found that explicitly passes trustAllCerts = true, and the accept-all hostname verifier (C8) is inferred from source.'], 'behavior_review': {'status': 'reviewed', 'review_contract_version': 23, 'regression_count': 0, 'patch_has_no_effect': False}}, 'digest_contract_assessment': {'security_relevance': 'false', 'contract_kind': 'unknown', 'expected_digest_source': '', 'backend_repository_available': False, 'backend_change_required': False, 'client_only_change_safe': False, 'rollout_strategy': '', 'pull_request_note': ''}, 'review_assumptions': ['Servers with self-signed or private-CA certificates will now be rejected unless their CA is installed on the device; the pipeline-provided network security config allows user-installed CAs.', 'Callers that omit trustAllCerts (ProviderAPI, provideOkHttpClient) are expected to work with platform validation.', 'The in-place edit keeps the public signature, so no caller edits are needed.', 'The existing hostnameVerifier call inside the trustAllCerts branch of setupSsl is left unchanged because the plan says to keep the explicit branch as it is.'], 'review_blockers': [], 'required_tests': [], 'decision': 'MULTI_FILE_FIX_PROPOSED_FOR_REVIEW', 'manual_review_required': True, 'auto_apply': False, 'publication_allowed': False, 'publication_status': 'blocked', 'semantic_validation': {'status': 'valid', 'errors': [], 'warnings': []}, 'stored_value_contract': {}, 'fix_scope': 'review_only', 'applied_for_validation': True, 'review_contract_version': 23, 'pr_attribution': {}, 'status': 'SUCCESS', 'error': None, 'original_method_body': '    trustAllCerts: Boolean = true,\n    connectTimeoutSecs: Long = 30L,', 'corrected_method_body': '    trustAllCerts: Boolean = false,\n    connectTimeoutSecs: Long = 30L,', 'finding_id': '6d0a3cf73013', 'branch': 'fix/setupssl-sslcontextspec-6d0a3cf73013-2ee36dcb4d', 'base_branch': 'main', 'base_commit': 'd2b979ccad9a3e54b9499929a9dc2824578b0fd9', 'solution_revision': '2ee36dcb4d', 'worktree_attempt': 1, 'orphaned_worktree_paths': [], 'worktree_path': '/home/antonow/cognalys_work/d_arm_sonnet_k3/pr_6d0a3cf73013_r1/worktrees/me.ash.reader.debug_47.apk/6d0a3cf73013/2ee36dcb4d', 'base_repository_path': '/home/antonow/cognalys_work/d_arm_sonnet_k3/pr_6d0a3cf73013_r1/clones/me.ash.reader.debug_47.apk', 'coordinated_edits': [{'source_file': 'app/src/main/java/me/ash/reader/infrastructure/di/OkHttpClientModule.kt', 'symbol': 'cachingHttpClient', 'edit_kind': 'declaration', 'original_code': '    trustAllCerts: Boolean = true,\n    connectTimeoutSecs: Long = 30L,', 'corrected_code': '    trustAllCerts: Boolean = false,\n    connectTimeoutSecs: Long = 30L,', 'reason': 'Make certificate validation the default; accept-all stays reachable only through an explicit trustAllCerts = true.'}, {'source_file': 'app/src/main/res/xml/network_security_config.xml', 'symbol': 'network_security_config.xml', 'edit_kind': 'create', 'original_code': '', 'corrected_code': '<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>\n<network-security-config>\n    <base-config cleartextTrafficPermitted="true">\n        <trust-anchors>\n            <certificates src="system" />\n            <certificates src="user" />\n        </trust-anchors>\n    </base-config>\n</network-security-config>\n', 'reason': "lets the system and user-installed CAs validate connections, so a self-hosted server's CA can be installed on the device; keeps cleartext allowed as the manifest had it"}, {'source_file': 'app/src/main/AndroidManifest.xml', 'symbol': 'AndroidManifest.xml', 'edit_kind': 'declaration', 'original_code': '<application\n        ', 'corrected_code': '<application\n        android:networkSecurityConfig="@xml/network_security_config"\n        ', 'reason': 'enables the network security config'}], 'changed_files': ['app/src/main/java/me/ash/reader/infrastructure/di/OkHttpClientModule.kt', 'app/src/main/res/xml/network_security_config.xml', 'app/src/main/AndroidManifest.xml'], 'quality_score': 90, 'explanation': '<!-- pr-title: Validate server certificates by default in cachingHttpClient -->\n`cachingHttpClient` in `OkHttpClientModule.kt` defaulted `trustAllCerts` to `true`. Callers that omit it (ProviderAPI, provideOkHttpClient) reached `setupSsl`, which passes an app-defined X509TrustManager with an empty `checkServerTrusted` to `SSLContext.init`, plus an accept-all hostname verifier. RVSec reported that the `TrustManager[]` given to `SSLContext.init` holds an app-defined manager and was not observed coming from a `TrustManagerFactory`. On the default path, no certificate validation happened.\n\nI changed the default to `trustAllCerts: Boolean = false`, so the existing validating branch (`Platform.get().platformTrustManager()`) is used. Accept-all is still reachable only by passing `trustAllCerts = true` explicitly.\n\nUsers of servers with self-signed or private-CA certificates will no longer connect unless that CA is installed on the device.', 'applied_timestamp': '2026-11-16T05:39:39.206106+00:00'}], 'errors': []}

